# Implementation clarity

This codebase contains stale comments, commented experiments, hard-coded dimensions, and partially completed branches. Before asserting behavior:

- trace the called function from the active entry point;
- inspect the relevant branch/commit when results are historical;
- distinguish CPU reference behavior from CUDA behavior;
- distinguish training from evaluation and check whether weights mutate;
- verify compiler flags before comparing performance;
- mark unresolved conclusions as audit flags rather than facts.

When multiple modern designs are possible, prefer the smallest change that preserves a clear historical comparison point.
